{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"event stream event stream","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md","fileName":"Event Stream.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Event Stream","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Event Sourcing and Projections]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Event Sourcing and Projections","Aggregate","Transaction Boundary","Optimistic Concurrency","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"event stream event stream","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md","fileName":"Event Stream.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Event Stream","heading":"Event Stream","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An event stream is an ordered sequence of events associated with a known identity, commonly one [[Aggregate]] instance. Events must be read in the same strict order in which they were written because replay uses that order to reconstruct state. A stream name can combine the aggregate type and identity. Appending to one stream forms the aggregate's [[Transaction Boundary]], and its revision supplies the expected version for [[Optimistic Concurrency]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Event Sourcing and Projections","Aggregate","Transaction Boundary","Optimistic Concurrency","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Event Stream.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"event stream event stream","filePath":"6 -